#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129271 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128848 :question/id #uuid "66d757d2-f2ad-5f0d-b4f1-8d426f4c8351" :question/math-academy-id "e-11579" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that maps the Cartesian $uvw$-space onto the Cartesian $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx = 2u-v,\\qquad\ny = u+3v+w,\\qquad\nz = u+2v-w.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{array} \\right]} \\to {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x ( u , v , w ) \\\\ y ( u , v , w ) \\\\ z ( u , v , w )\\end{array} \\right]},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf T,$ denoted $\\dfrac{\\partial (x, y, z)}{\\partial (u, v, w)} ,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =3 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =2 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(-3-2)+(-1-1) \\\\  & =-10-2 \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d433063f-f145-5bf4-8bd4-8d5e5b36b3d8" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048219 :topic/difficulty 0.5901295644710777 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428534 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex 