 " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323999} {:answer/id #uuid "350992e5-036c-535c-8a4b-6a5ab4c6fa16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324405} {:answer/id #uuid "81e74165-da06-5f93-ae92-aeef9db19857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325063} {:answer/id #uuid "a528987d-54c7-5615-ae6d-cbc6a9db0c60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325376} {:answer/id #uuid "efd74025-7232-59ef-bfa0-45a2a9dfad28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a528987d-54c7-5615-ae6d-cbc6a9db0c60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325376} :answer-field/id #uuid "60477555-dd44-54e5-9698-cd175b7154c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326385}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24830b7e-b0be-5ebb-9a57-2cd58c40cf8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-39299" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +v\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=v\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=w.\n$$\n\nYou may assume that $\\theta $ is a fixed constant." :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 0 \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01c262fc-9bb7-50e9-9bd9-71220d222eee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323988} {:answer/id #uuid "1f7284f1-bddd-57c4-bee7-4e81f853fddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2vw\\operatorname{cos}⁡(vw)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324235} {:answer/id #uuid "45d58fec-b6fd-54bf-819d-1320f8bbad5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4vw" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324536} {:answer/id #uuid "5a92451e-4ced-5c86-9ad8-ed111fb7bb27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4vw\\operatorname{cos}⁡(vw)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324719} {:answer/id #uuid "b55d6eaa-09cc-570c-89c0-c7bfca63934e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b55d6eaa-09cc-570c-89c0-c7bfca63934e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325531} :answer-field/id #uuid "785a8a4c-9863-5dc4-b03a-b4c3232d979e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326437}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "045d5f30-3ffc-5bb0-bb67-dd9e010fc71b" :question/math-academy-id "q-39666" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4v \\\\ 3{u}^{2}+2\\operatorname{cos}(vw) \\\\ vw\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=4v,\\,y(u,v,w)=3{u}^{2}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(vw),\\,z(u,v,w)=vw.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =4 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =6u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-2w\\operatorname{sin}⁡(vw) & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =-2v\\operatorname{sin}⁡(vw) \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =w, & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 6u & -2w\\operatorname{sin}⁡(vw) & -2v\\operatorname{sin}⁡(vw) \\\\ 0 & w & v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4(-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}6u & -2v\\operatorname{sin}⁡(vw) \\\\ 0 & v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-4(6uv-0) \\\\  & =-24uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46d3639c-107c-558c-b1c4-6ddd7cb81df1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{u}^{3}v-{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279222} {:answer/id #uuid "58a20343-ced5-57fc-b813-e98d7f250092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v(3{u}^{2}+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279406} {:answer/id #uuid "59f8ccb9-adf9-523b-b70b-b84e01b6cdc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{u}^{3}-v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279416} {:answer/id #uuid "ba0b239b-6293-5a6c-a399-4c20fbd9ba89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280232} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d8a949-98c9-53b2-a5c0-d91ecebaaf5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-u{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59f8ccb9-adf9-523b-b70b-b84e01b6cdc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{u}^{3}-v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279416} :answer-field/id #uuid "095a93fc-962d-5e7a-8222-89b127de9857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280849}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba1e3545-8702-5a08-88b1-f7be09c82e4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161792" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx=u{v}^{2}+w,\\,y={u}^{3}+v,\\,z=uv.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={v}^{2} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =2uv & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =3{u}^{2} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =u & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}{v}^{2} & 2uv & 1 \\\\ 3{u}^{2} & 1 & 0 \\\\ v & u & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}3{u}^{2} & 1 \\\\ v & u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3{u}^{3}-v.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39a3a5e9-764a-5e8b-8b50-93add8b3fc05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{w}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279099} {:answer/id #uuid "723714f3-b594-566d-a56e-12b3c635b92e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{w}(1+u)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279630} {:answer/id #uuid "790dd6b1-fb1b-55ce-8d23-99d906744d93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-uw{e}^{u+w}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279671} {:answer/id #uuid "b3690af9-7cf0-5336-b7d4-e7c30102fb21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{u+v}-3{e}^{w}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280174} {:answer/id #uuid "f77275e3-e3d3-5b1d-ad31-9113451a2bec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3w{e}^{u+v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "723714f3-b594-566d-a56e-12b3c635b92e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{w}(1+u)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279630} :answer-field/id #uuid "d23defb7-252c-5ea7-b5af-33ad4ec74ab1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281204}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10460eec-f814-5d84-b88f-d89f8f558989" :question/math-academy-id "q-161793" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u{e}^{w} \\\\ w-u \\\\ w{e}^{u}-3v\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u{e}^{w},\\,y(u,v,w)=w-u,\\,z(u,v,w)=w{e}^{u}-3v.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{w} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =u{e}^{w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =w{e}^{u} & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =-3, & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & ={e}^{u}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}{e}^{w} & 0 & u{e}^{w} \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ w{e}^{u} & -3 & {e}^{u}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)(-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}{e}^{w} & u{e}^{w} \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3({e}^{w}+u{e}^{w}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{w}(1+u).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07db5547-d099-5a39-ad82-abc875d51fab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(u-v)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278662} {:answer/id #uuid "273f9725-21b0-51ad-aa3e-3681dbe69685" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278942} {:answer/id #uuid "5643486d-15ec-545d-a303-f0e9cc3db1be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279382} {:answer/id #uuid "5a7bc25d-f032-5290-9eff-ce5cbada276f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6u-2v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279426} {:answer/id #uuid "848acec7-1e41-5ca9-b95e-cefaaa4e11e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5643486d-15ec-545d-a303-f0e9cc3db1be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279382} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea688683-0e2b-5e81-8438-0d34494b3330" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281250}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "27f802ec-0d96-5c3f-9520-b80524648c50" :question/math-academy-id "q-161794" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2} \\\\ u+3w \\\\ -v\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)={u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,y(u,v,w)=u+3w,\\,z(u,v,w)=-v.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =2v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =3 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =-1, & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 2v & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)(-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =6u-0 \\\\  & =6u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "555199b9-aced-5dd0-a7a4-1c3b529e0ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{w}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279370} {:answer/id #uuid "71d28527-0b0f-581a-b145-41b591816c80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{uv}{w}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279625} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf35eb4-7d06-504d-97d6-6d62c0d12660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279976} {:answer/id #uuid "9e2827ef-81bc-5319-a0af-3f83476042b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{u}{w}-\\frac{1}{v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279995} {:answer/id #uuid "f447c433-d789-5722-828c-42983f30e64f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{u}{w}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f447c433-d789-5722-828c-42983f30e64f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{u}{w}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280731} :answer-field/id #uuid "65c51ca4-49aa-5089-b98e-4e0fed70679a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281007}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "590673d5-674e-5f87-8a3b-a26381077e85" :question/math-academy-id "q-161796" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}(u\\hspace{0.167em}v\\hspace{0.167em}w) \\\\ u+2w \\\\ uv\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u\\,v\\,w),\\,y(u,v,w)=u+2w,\\,z(u,v,w)=uv.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =\\frac{1}{u} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =\\frac{1}{v} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =\\frac{1}{w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =u & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{1}{u} & \\frac{1}{v} & \\frac{1}{w} \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ v & u & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{w}(-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ v & u\\end{vmatrix}+2(-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{1}{u} & \\frac{1}{v} \\\\ v & u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{w}(u-0)-2(1-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{u}{w}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406772 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03b82058-2ed1-5ab3-8be0-f2ccd9e791be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv-2u{v}^{2}-vu" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406759} {:answer/id #uuid "2b07851c-5666-5e08-93b4-ea52710578c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}-2{v}^{3}-vw" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406761} {:answer/id #uuid "4e04d287-7eaa-501d-ba5e-706a25e1adcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2vw" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406764} {:answer/id #uuid "78a6574d-a7a7-5dd3-9372-265b4fd8dfa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv-2u{v}^{2}+vu" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406765} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d7dba0-5d86-5a7b-97ed-55ed0cf1cb1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}-2{v}^{3}+vw" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b07851c-5666-5e08-93b4-ea52710578c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}-2{v}^{3}-vw" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406761} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc7e9e1f-8201-5457-9ae8-866cb0a50e5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406770}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9eac1497-79c1-5ed3-be68-00cfa0edfef5" :question/math-academy-id "q-39710" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}+vw,\\,y=2-uv,\\,z={v}^{2}-w.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =2v & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2u & w & v \\\\ -v & -u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2u(-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-u & 0 \\\\ 2v & -1\\end{vmatrix}+(-v)(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}w & v \\\\ 2v & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2u(u-0)+v(-w-2{v}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}-2{v}^{3}-vw.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424178 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09c7d7c2-430d-5af8-9d05-fa5665e62862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424149} {:answer/id #uuid "6f2a26b3-3177-579e-877d-0fe20ffae536" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424158} {:answer/id #uuid "9406cdae-72e2-5c66-8ad2-f1e16969ae1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424162} {:answer/id #uuid "af88273c-a488-5b6d-af48-680f8f2c6cda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424163} {:answer/id #uuid "de9aadb1-15c7-5202-b107-ef067be5cce6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09c7d7c2-430d-5af8-9d05-fa5665e62862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424149} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d447ea2-8560-5077-b8b9-f3304d7a91d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424173}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03a9f960-3754-59ca-a7ce-a0ebf6a90fdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-39294" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx=v+w,\\,y=u+w,\\,z=u+v.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+1(-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)(0-1)+(1-0) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "146610e3-5c1c-5561-9ca3-9774666c6c05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-a-b-c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424150} {:answer/id #uuid "4d3fd2ac-fcea-50a9-92dd-45cccffc9e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-abc" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424155} {:answer/id #uuid "5938eea0-a7c5-5a7f-bf1f-a9fd0efaaf3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a+b+c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424157} {:answer/id #uuid "7a38c64c-896b-5232-a5e4-465265d40434" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "abc" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424161} {:answer/id #uuid "b5179334-ac94-5f42-8f5c-8c9ece45c7a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a38c64c-896b-5232-a5e4-465265d40434" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "abc" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424161} :answer-field/id #uuid "3708f8e2-7d98-51bd-8b21-20ee27c9855a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424174}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0fc3f590-a25e-51e5-80e8-0d05b569e022" :question/math-academy-id "q-39664" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx=au,\\,y=bv,\\,z=cw.\n$$\n\nYou may assume that $a$, $b$ and $c$ are fixed constants." :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =a & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =b & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}a & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & b & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & c\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =a(-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}b & 0 \\\\ 0 & c\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =a(bc-0) \\\\  & =abc.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01f1e83f-e91e-5090-bc9c-c0d8a5b24dec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+\\operatorname{sin}⁡w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509699} {:answer/id #uuid "30cff47c-46a9-5910-9362-18ed14cc8d58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509792} {:answer/id #uuid "47299991-0c88-52f8-adac-83f8c4229c9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509831} {:answer/id #uuid "87f9ca78-e7eb-5c39-bc73-ffb1b08282b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509983} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a8b398-e764-5a3f-9020-8353ddf15a9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+{sin}^{2}⁡u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87f9ca78-e7eb-5c39-bc73-ffb1b08282b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509983} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d0df2e4-d380-5912-bac6-465760a259a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510257}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30a2be53-ad1e-54e7-8cc2-2924faaf8e17" :question/math-academy-id "q-161795" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+\\operatorname{cos}w \\\\ v \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}u+w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u+\\operatorname{cos}⁡w,\\,y(u,v,w)=v,\\,z(u,v,w)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u+w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡w \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0, & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡w \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡w \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡w.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65eac0db-4498-5219-a599-16571ff5b0ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509900} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ee05e3-c0ef-572d-b71a-0521af7c7c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510151} {:answer/id #uuid "e13473ff-e770-5bc2-84cc-d2f5a63a463b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510166} {:answer/id #uuid "ec060073-eee0-5eb4-a23b-64f1baba3d7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510197} {:answer/id #uuid "f40d8dc6-4b68-5931-af1a-b12969faf5dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65eac0db-4498-5219-a599-16571ff5b0ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509900} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d304d66-3b35-5b7a-a10d-e4c98f3bf8ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510303}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db419926-6089-5205-b99f-0938320c28f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-161799" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+v\\operatorname{cos}\\theta +w\\operatorname{sin}\\theta  \\\\ 3v \\\\ u\\operatorname{sin}\\theta +w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nYou may assume that $\\theta $ is a fixed constant." :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u+v\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +w\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y(u,v,w)=3v,\\,z(u,v,w)=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =3 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0, & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =3{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538080 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44333139-cdf6-5139-b942-4aef72fea8fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24 u \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538076} {:answer/id #uuid "6d411a6c-64a4-53c2-8f4e-1505fb27596f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 24 u^{2} \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538084} {:answer/id #uuid "aafe06af-f994-53ab-b2f9-00ddee90e21f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24 u^{2} \\sin{\\left(v \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(v \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538093} {:answer/id #uuid "bd61b5ac-cd11-592e-bc2f-458d8703fe2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24 u^{2} \\sin^{3}{\\left(v \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538096} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b1e996-8fcc-5b36-9cb4-719bfe1f008e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24 u^{2} \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7b1e996-8fcc-5b36-9cb4-719bfe1f008e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24 u^{2} \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538103} :answer-field/id #uuid "697c4afa-b74b-58e9-8673-20fb02c283a6" :answer-field/key "